@@ -54,6 +54,8 @@ audit log.
 - `merchandise` is the sum of the lines.
 - `adjustments` come off the merchandise before tax. Each has a `kind`:
   - `employee`: staff get their `employee_discount_percent` off the merchandise.
+  - `discount_code`: a discount code entered at checkout. The description says
+    which code, e.g. `"SUMMER20: 20% off"`.
   - `loyalty`: redeemed loyalty points.
 - Prices include VAT, so `tax` is the VAT included in the total.
 - Shipping is £4.95, and free when the merchandise, before adjustments, is at
@@ -73,3 +75,7 @@ Staff create codes with `POST /admin/discount-codes`:
 
 A code that's already taken is a `409`. The response has the code's `kind`,
 which is `percent` for now.
+
+Customers use a code by passing `discount_code` to `POST /checkout`. One code
+per order, and it combines with employee discounts and loyalty points; each
+percentage is of the merchandise. An unknown or expired code is a `422`.
diff --git a/shop/api/routes/orders.py b/shop/api/routes/orders.py
